Overview
The Personalized Education Assistant is designed to empower learners of all levels—beginner, intermediate, and advanced—by providing a structured and customized learning journey. It leverages the Groq API for generating intelligent content and the Serper API for real-time web search to curate up-to-date resources. The application is built using Streamlit, offering an intuitive and interactive user interface.
Key functionalities include:

Generating sequential learning paths for multiple topics.
Curating learning materials tailored to user expertise.
Creating progressive quizzes to test knowledge.
Suggesting practical, industry-relevant project ideas.

This tool is ideal for self-learners, educators, or anyone seeking a structured approach to mastering new skills.

Features

Sequential Learning Path:

Generate a step-by-step learning plan for multiple topics.
Tasks include clear titles, detailed descriptions, learning objectives, and estimated completion times.
Tracks task completion status.


Content Curation:

Combines AI-generated recommendations with real-time web search results.
Provides core concepts, learning progression paths, study approaches, key skills, and solutions to common challenges.
Displays top web resources with titles, links, and snippets.


Quiz Generator:

Creates customizable quizzes with progressive difficulty.
Includes multiple-choice questions, correct answers, and explanations.
Supports 3 to 10 questions per quiz, tailored to the user’s expertise level.


Project Ideas Generator:

Suggests engaging, level-appropriate project ideas aligned with current industry trends.
Includes project titles, descriptions, technologies/concepts, timelines, learning outcomes, and step-by-step outlines.
Optionally incorporates user interests for personalization.


User-Friendly Interface:

Built with Streamlit for a responsive, tab-based layout.
Features API key validation, model selection, and connection testing.
Provides real-time feedback with spinners and success/error messages.




Technologies Used

Python 3.8+: Core programming language.
Streamlit: Web application framework for the user interface.
Groq API: AI-powered content generation (models: LLaMA3, Mixtral, Gemma).
Serper API: Real-time Google search for learning resources.
Requests: HTTP requests for API communication.
Dataclasses & Enums: For structured data modeling.
Typing: For type-hinted, maintainable code.


Installation
Follow these steps to set up the project locally:

Clone the Repository:
git clone https://github.com/your-username/personalized-education-assistant.git
cd personalized-education-assistant


Create a Virtual Environment:
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate


Install Dependencies:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Sample requirements.txt:
streamlit==1.38.0
requests==2.32.3


Set Up API Keys:

Obtain a Groq API key from Groq Console.
Obtain a Serper API key from Serper.dev.
These will be entered via the application’s sidebar during runtime.


Run the Application:
streamlit run app.py

The app will open in your default browser at http://localhost:8501.



Configuration

API Keys:

Enter your Groq API Key and Serper API Key in the sidebar.
Validate the connection using the “Test API Connection” button.


Model Selection:

Choose from available Groq models (e.g., llama3-8b-8192, llama3-70b-8192, mixtral-8x7b-32768, gemma-7b-it).
Default: llama3-8b-8192.


Error Handling:

The app provides detailed error messages for API issues, network failures, or JSON parsing errors.
Check API credits and key validity if errors persist.




Usage

Access the Application:

Open the app in your browser.
Configure API keys and select a model in the sidebar.


Navigate Tabs:

Learning Path: Enter topics (one per line) and select an expertise level to generate a learning plan.
Content Curation: Input a topic and expertise level to get AI recommendations and web resources.
Quiz Generator: Specify a topic, expertise level, and number of questions to create a quiz.
Project Ideas: Provide a topic, expertise level, and optional interests to receive project suggestions.


Interact with Results:

Expand tasks, view curated content, read quiz questions, or explore project ideas.
Mark learning tasks as complete for progress tracking.


Troubleshooting:

Ensure API keys are valid and have sufficient credits.
Check internet connectivity for API requests.
Refer to error messages for specific issues.




Project Structure
personalized-education-assistant/
│
├── app.py                 # Main Streamlit application
├── requirements.txt       # Python dependencies
├── README.md              # Project documentation
└── venv/                  # Virtual environment (not tracked)

Key components in app.py:

Config: Stores API URLs.
ExpertiseLevel: Enum for learner levels (Beginner, Intermediate, Advanced).
LearningTask: Dataclass for task structure.
GroqClient: Handles Groq API interactions.
SerperClient: Manages Serper API searches.
PersonalizedEducationAssistant: Core logic for learning paths, curation, quizzes, and projects.
main(): Streamlit UI and tab-based navigation.


